# Atomic variables & concurrent collections

## Atomic variables — lock-free single value

```java
AtomicInteger count = new AtomicInteger(0);
count.incrementAndGet();   // atomic read-add-write, no lock
```

Backed by **compare-and-swap** in hardware — optimistic, retries instead of blocking. `updateAndGet` runs any function in that loop.

Protects **one** variable only; two atomics together are not atomic.

## Concurrent collections

- **`ConcurrentHashMap`** — the workhorse; concurrent reads + writes
- **`CopyOnWriteArrayList`** — read-mostly (listeners)
- **`BlockingQueue`** — producer/consumer; `take()` blocks for an item

## Compound ops must stay atomic

```java
// BROKEN — both threads pass the check:
if (!map.containsKey(k)) map.put(k, compute(k));

// atomic — one operation:
map.computeIfAbsent(k, this::compute);
map.merge(word, 1, Integer::sum);   // concurrent tally
```

**Prefer ready-made tools over hand-rolled locks.**
